@participant9 any chance you could [produce a bugreport](BUG-1b7641a16971a9cd75822c0ed8043fee70ae88cf05c52981dc220eb96a5c49a8-20210427151443Z-fbcd4fd3a4b7ad94
) from the Ingress proxy Pod at the time when it is failing and show us the `Ingress` and backend `Service` config as well as what command you are running that fails?

Additionally - are you also on k3s?

@participant13 thank you for the detailed description and bug reports.
I skimmed through the logs and I think I only saw the proxy receive traffic on port 80. We only expose port 443 to tailnet (and we don't redirect 80 -> 443)

Could you confirm that you see the issue if you explicitly call 443/https i.e `curl -vv https://<redacted-host>`?
